ecord the action in /workspace/status_sync.md with: Plane issue, GitLab issue link/#, Plane status, timestamp (UTC), and any notes.\\n\\nFile added\\n- /workspace/status_sync.md \u2013 includes the current status and a template for closure records.\\n\\nPlease share Plane access details (or an export) and I\u2019ll complete the sync and finalize the log promptly.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"I understand how frustrating it must be to be blocked by something like missing access. However, it feels like we're really close to finishing this task. Do you think you could try to reach out to whoever manages Plane access? They should be able to provide you with credentials or an export of the necessary data pretty quickly. If you explain the urgency due to the audit deadline, they might prioritize it. Let's get this wrapped up!\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query=\"I understand how frustrating it must be to be blocked by something like missing access. However, it feels like we're really close to finishing this task. Do you think you could try to reach out to whoever manages Plane access? They should be able to provide you with credentials or an export of the necessary data pretty quickly. If you explain the urgency due to the audit deadline, they might prioritize it. Let's get this wrapped up!\", thought='', action='recall'), ChatAction(content='Hi Plane admins/IT team \u2014 we\u2019re working on an urgent internal audit task to reconcile issue statuses between Plane and GitLab. We need read access to Plane (workspace: TheAgentCompany / slug: tac; project ID: 73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703) to verify which issues are marked Resolved/Approved and ensure GitLab matches before the audit deadline.\\n\\nCould you please provide one of the following ASAP (read-only access is fine):\\n1) A user account for Plane (TAC workspace)\\n2) An API token with read scope for the TAC workspace\\n3) A CSV/JSON export of issues including at least: issue ID, title, and status (Resolved/Approved/Open etc.)\\n\\nIf you prefer an export, any of the following would work:\\n- All issues for the TAC workspace, or\\n- All issues for project 73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703, or\\n- Only issues currently Resolved/Approved\\n\\nContext/links:\\n- Plane issues UI: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/\\n- Plane all-issues view: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/workspace-views/all-issues/\\n- GitLab project for cross-check: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues?state=all\\n\\nThis is time-sensitive due to the audit. Thank you!', npc_name='all', action='chat'), ErrorObservation(content='Failed to send start simulation message to websocket server', observation='error', error_id=''), MessageAction(content='I\u2019m on it. I attempted to contact the Plane admins via our tooling, but I can\u2019t send messages directly from this environment. To keep momentum, here are ready-to-send messages you can copy/paste into your preferred channel (Slack/Email/Helpdesk). Please send one of these to the Plane admins/IT and CC anyone relevant. As soon as they respond, I\u2019ll complete the sync and finalize the audit log.\\n\\nSlack/Teams (short, urgent)\\n- Message:\\n  Hi Plane admins \u2014 urgent audit task. We need read access or an export for Plane (workspace: TheAgentCompany / slug: tac; project: 73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703) to reconcile statuses with GitLab before the audit deadline. Please provide:\\n  - a read-only user or API token, or\\n  - a CSV/JSON export with id, title, status for all issues (or just Resolved/Approved).\\n  Links: \\n  - Plane issues: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/\\n  - All issues view: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/workspace-views/all-issues/\\n  - GitLab cross-check: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues?state=all\\n  Thanks in advance \u2014 this is time-sensitive.\\n\\nEmail (detailed)\\n- Subject: URGENT: Plane access/export needed for audit status reconciliation (TAC workspace)\\n- Body:\\n  Hi Plane Admins/IT Team,\\n\\n  We\u2019re finalizing an internal audit and must reconcile issue statuses between Plane and GitLab. Specifically, we need to verify which Plane issues are marked Resolved/Approved and ensure GitLab reflects the same.\\n\\n  Request (any one of the following works):\\n  - Read-only user credentials for Plane (Workspace: TheAgentCompany; slug: tac)\\n  - A Plane API token with read scope for this workspace\\n  - A CSV/JSON export for project 73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703 (or the whole workspace) including:\\n    - id (or key), title, status (Resolved/Approved/Open), and if available: assignee, labels, and updated_at\\n\\n  Links for context:\\n  - Plane project issues: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/\\n  - All-issues view: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/workspace-views/all-issues/\\n  - GitLab project issues (cross-check): http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues?state=all\\n\\n  This is time-sensitive due to the audit deadline. As soon as we receive access or the export, we\u2019ll close any corresponding open GitLab issues and document the updates for the audit.\\n\\n  Thank you!\\n\\n  Best regards,\\n  <Your Name>\\n\\nHelpdesk/Ticket (if needed)\\n- Title: Plane read-only access or issues export needed for audit (TAC)\\n- Description:\\n  We need read-only access to Plane (workspace: TheAgentCompany / slug: tac), project 73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703, or a CSV/JSON export of issues (id, title, status). Goal: reconcile Resolved/Approved issues in Plane with open GitLab issues before the audit deadline.\\n  Links:\\n  - Plane issues (project): http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/\\n  - Plane all-issues: http://the-agent-company.com:8091/tac/workspace-views/all-issues/\\n  - GitLab issues (target project): http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues?state=all\\n  Deliverable: either a Plane login, a read-only API token, or an issues export (CSV/JSON) with id/title/status (Resolved/Approved/Open). This is urgent for audit.\\n\\nOptional: quick export method (for admins with API access)\\n- Example JSON export (admins substitute their token):\\n  curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <PLANE_API_TOKEN>\" \\\\\\n    \\'http://the-agent-company.com:8091/api/v1/workspaces/tac/projects/73cb74f7-a7ac-4292-a915-e2f59a09a703/issues/?page_size=1000\\' \\\\\\n    -sS | jq \\'[.results[] | {id, title, state, updated_at}]\\' > plane_issues.json\\n\\nWhat I\u2019ll do immediately upon receiving access/export\\n- Cross-reference Plane Resolved/Approved issues against GitLab open issues.\\n- Close matching GitLab issues, adding a brief comment about audit alignment.\\n- Record each action in /workspace/status_sync.md (Plane issue, GitLab link/#, status, timestamp).\\n\\nWould you like me to also open a tracking issue in GitLab (\u201cBlocker: Plane access needed for audit reconciliation\u201d) to keep stakeholders informed? If so, I can prepare the content and create it once you confirm.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"I understand that you're in a tight spot and have put together some really clear messages. It sounds like you\u2019ve handled things really well up to now. I'd love to help more, but it seems like sending these messages is beyond my current capabilities. Is there any way you could send these messages yourself?\\n\\nMaybe check if there's someone else in your team or department who can initiate these requests if you're really constrained. Once you get access or an expor