 this in /workspace/status_sync.md.\\n\\n2) Attempted to sign into Plane using the provided GitLab credentials\\n- Navigated to the Plane sign-in and issues pages and attempted to proceed with root / theagentcompany.\\n- The login did not complete; Plane appears to require distinct credentials (or SSO we don\u2019t have). I did not brute-force or retry beyond the single cautious attempt you approved.\\n- Without Plane access, I still can\u2019t read which issues are Resolved/Approved to safely close corresponding GitLab issues.\\n\\nCurrent status\\n- Blocker officially documented in GitLab (issue #4167).\\n- status_sync.md updated with the blocker link and current state.\\n- No GitLab issues were closed yet pending Plane verification (to avoid mismatches).\\n\\nWhat I recommend next\\n- Please send one of the prepared messages to the Plane admins/IT (Slack/Email/Helpdesk) to request either:\\n  - a read-only Plane account for TAC, or\\n  - a read-only API token, or\\n  - a CSV/JSON export of issues (id, title, status).\\n- As soon as I receive access or an export, I will:\\n  - Cross-check Plane\u2019s Resolved/Approved issues with GitLab\u2019s open issues,\\n  - Close matches in GitLab with an audit note,\\n  - Record each action in /workspace/status_sync.md.\\n\\nIf you want, I can also keep the GitLab blocker issue updated with any replies/actions as they come in.', image_urls=None, wait_for_response=True, action='message', security_risk=None), MessageAction(content=\"Thank you for handling this so efficiently. You've documented everything thoroughly and taken logical steps to mitigate the blocker.\\n\\nThe next step would definitely be to get someone to send one of those messages to the Plane admins or IT to get the access or export you need. Unfortunately, I can\u2019t send external messages, but you might consider:\\n\\n1. **Finding a colleague who can send the message:** Explain the urgency and ask if they can send one of the pre-written messages on your behalf.\\n2. **Using any internal communication tools:** If there's an internal messaging system you have access to, try reaching out through that.\\n\\nAs soon as you get the required access or export, it sounds like you\u2019re all set to finish syncing the statuses. Please keep the GitLab blocker issue updated with progress to ensure everyone\u2019s in the loop. Let's get this over the finish line!\", image_urls=None, wait_for_response=False, action='message', security_risk=None), RecallAction(recall_type='knowledge', query=\"Thank you for handling this so efficiently. You've documented everything thoroughly and taken logical steps to mitigate the blocker.\\n\\nThe next step would definitely be to get someone to send one of those messages to the Plane admins or IT to get the access or export you need. Unfortunately, I can\u2019t send external messages, but you might consider:\\n\\n1. **Finding a colleague who can send the message:** Explain the urgency and ask if they can send one of the pre-written messages on your behalf.\\n2. **Using any internal communication tools:** If there's an internal messaging system you have access to, try reaching out through that.\\n\\nAs soon as you get the required access or export, it sounds like you\u2019re all set to finish syncing the statuses. Please keep the GitLab blocker issue updated with progress to ensure everyone\u2019s in the loop. Let's get this over the finish line!\", thought='', action='recall'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/openhands/-/issues/4167')\\nnoop(1500)\\nfill('nonexistent', 'x')\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  * In this project \\n\\n    * [ New issue  ](/root/openhands/-/issues/new)\\n    * [ New merge request  ](/root/openhands/-/merge_requests/new)\\